## Scoring Rubric

Score each opportunity 0–5 on the dimensions below, then weight. Anything below the threshold doesn't get a bid.

| Dimension | Weight | What "5" looks like | What "0" looks like |
|---|---|---|---|
| Work type | 25% | Tier A — build a lifecycle program, advisory, audit + roadmap | Tier D — sporadic task work |
| Client size & resourcing | 20% | $2M+ revenue, funded startup, team in place to execute | Solo founder, no list, no budget signals |
| Industry fit | 15% | DTC, CPG, e-commerce, ICP match | Niche B2B, services, irrelevant vertical |
| Budget fit | 15% | $2K–$4K fixed (or hourly that maps there over 30–45 days) | Sub-$500 budget, "looking for the cheapest option" |
| Engagement length | 10% | 30–45 day project with clear ongoing potential | One-and-done, hours-only |
| Tool/expertise alignment | 10% | Klaviyo, ActiveCampaign, Omnisend, HubSpot, lifecycle/automation | Tool I don't work in or generic "email help" |
| Strategic upside | 5% | Repeatable buyer profile, referral potential, case study material | Anonymous one-off, no relationship runway |

**Bid thresholds:**

- **Score 4.0+** → Priority bid. Send a tailored proposal same day.
- **Score 3.0–3.9** → Bid if quota allows; use a short, sharp proposal.
- **Score 2.0–2.9** → Skip unless something compensating jumps out (e.g., a known brand).
- **Score below 2.0** → Auto-skip.

