## Pipeline Math (Sanity Check)

To land $15K/month at $2K–$4K per project:

- ~5 new projects/month at $3K average → $15K
- Assume a 1-in-5 bid-to-hire conversion at the priority tier → ~25 priority bids/month → ~6 priority bids/week
- This is only realistic if the filter is tight. Bidding 50/week on mediocre fits hits the connect budget without lifting close rate.

If the priority feed isn't generating ~6 fits/week, the filter is too narrow OR the search keywords need expanding — not the bar lowering.

---

## Review Cadence

- **Weekly:** Review which bids were accepted vs. ignored. Update keyword and negative-keyword lists.
- **Monthly:** Re-score the rubric against actual won/lost work. If a "3.5" client turned into the best engagement of the quarter, the weights are wrong.
- **Quarterly:** Refresh the ICP table with new anchor clients won.
